# OnlyTravelers — environment
#
# Nothing here is required. The app ships with its own maps, drawn from real
# boundary data, and links out to Google Maps by name and by coordinate. The
# key below only adds the embedded, pannable map on a destination page.

# Google Maps Embed API key.
#
# Get one at https://console.cloud.google.com/google/maps-apis — enable the
# "Maps Embed API" for the project. NEXT_PUBLIC_ means this value is compiled
# into the browser bundle and is readable by anyone, so it MUST be restricted
# in the Google Cloud console:
#   - Application restriction: HTTP referrers, listing only your own domains.
#   - API restriction: Maps Embed API only.
# An unrestricted key on a public site is someone else's bill.
#
# Leave it unset and destination pages fall back to our own map plus the
# "open in Google Maps" links, which work for everyone with no key at all.
NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=

# Map tiles for the accurate (pannable) maps on state and destination pages.
#
# Default: the public OpenStreetMap tile servers, which need no key and are
# fine for a launch. Their usage policy
# (https://operations.osmfoundation.org/policies/tiles/) is for light use,
# not a high-traffic commercial site — before that, point this at a tile
# provider (MapTiler, Stadia, Thunderforest, a self-hosted server…) and set
# the attribution they require. {z}/{x}/{y} are substituted by the map.
NEXT_PUBLIC_MAP_TILES_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_MAP_TILES_ATTRIBUTION=
